      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-13T20:43:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is failing to create a feature a normal signal or an error case? It looks like an error case, and if so, we might want to be emphatic about it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 186,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "8794dc069e6a1a5a8b5f2f364012c414bd11b556",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88abb038_a08b77b9",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/internal/ImsService.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-13T23:42:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It definitely isn\u0027t expected. This is an error case, however, there is no way for us to stop them. We already handle null in the framework. Technically, the base implementation for these features return null. If the framework was to accidentally try to create a feature for a feature that the Implementation wasn\u0027t expecting, null will be returned. \n\nI can put an error log message.",
      "parentUuid": "40f5886a_0e253c91",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 186,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "8794dc069e6a1a5a8b5f2f364012c414bd11b556",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
